      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The 2011 US involvement in Libya, largely a support for the \"Arab Spring\" and a \"responsibility to protect\" (RtoP) mandate for the Gaddafi regime.\nWhile the UN concluded it was a \"success\" for the intervention in 2011 as it led to the end of Gaddafi and a period of political stability for the UN.\nFrom a  geopolitical perspective, the intervention is now often debated as a \" failure \" because the weak political and economic outcome left the country in a state of political and ethnic conflict.\nThis \" soft \" failure in the pro is a \" challenge \" for the \" UN \" and the \" international \" \" community \" in \" the \" \" \" \" \" \" U \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \" \"",
